<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Forte di Belvedere</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1590">1590</a>–<a href="/years/1595">1595</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Forte di Belvedere is a fortress on the Boboli hill above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, built in 1590–1595 for Grand Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinando-i-de-medici">Ferdinando I de' Medici</a> to designs attributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardo-buontalenti">Bernardo Buontalenti</a>. Overlooking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pitti-palace">Pitti Palace</a> and the city, it was meant both to defend Florence and to secure the Medici against internal revolt, and it reportedly held the dynasty's treasure. It is now used for exhibitions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/forte-di-belvedere.jpg" alt="Forte di Belvedere" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Forte_belvedere,_edificio_principale_07.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
